  "notes": "<div><font size=\"5\"><b>Effects</b></font></div><div>Four moving heads from the fixture library, eight PARs and two LED bars of eight cells, and an effect of every kind. An effect is worked out anew all the time from a shape and a few values, instead of steps that are stored.</div><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">What is in it</font></b></div><ul><li>Effects 1 and 2 move the heads: a circle, and a fan of pan swings (two wings, mirrored).</li><li>Effects 3 and 4 let the PARs rise and fall: a chase (a sine spread over them), and a pulse in blocks of two.</li><li>Effects 5 and 6 change the color of the PARs: a rainbow, and red and blue.</li><li>Effects 7 to 10 paint the two bars by where their cells are on the stage: bars, a ripple, sparkle and plasma.</li><li>Memories 1 and 4 point the heads, 2 lights the PARs blue, 3 the bars warm. The stack plays the effects as a show.</li></ul><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">Try it</font></b></div><ol><li>Open <b>Effects</b>. A key brings the fader of its effect up, which starts it, or down, which stops it; the fader sets how much of the effect there is. The name under a key chooses it for the editor and the preview, and the key of an empty number offers the kinds to make a new one.</li><li>Start effect 3 (Chase): the PARs come up white, one after the other. Push memory 2 up on <b>Main</b>: the PARs are blue now, and the chase only shows where it is brighter than the look.</li><li>Start effect 5 (Rainbow): it takes over the color of the PARs. Stop the chase: the rainbow stays, at the brightness memory 2 gives. Take memory 2 down: now the rainbow lights the PARs itself, as bright as its fader.</li><li>Push memory 1 up and start effect 1: the heads circle around where memory 1 points them, and on <b>Stage</b> a beam from each head shows where it points. Push memory 4 up: they circle around that.</li><li>Move <b>Speed</b>, <b>Size</b> and <b>Spread</b> while an effect runs: they change this run only. <b>Keep</b> stores them in the effect, ↺ takes its own values again.</li><li>On <b>Stage</b>, the bars show effects 7 to 10. Press <b>Stack</b> and <b>GO</b> through the show.</li></ol><div>For keys of the effects on Main, show some in <b>Settings</b>: effect keys of the independents, and a row of effect faders under the memories.</div>",
